tion" class="sc-fvxzrP bFKOnZ pf-26_"><div style="--cw:1000px" class="sc-jQrDum heCnGO"><div class="sc-bBHxTw QejWU pf-27_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-hOGkXu krzkQM pf-28_"><h2 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-gWXbKe iZtXJr pf-29_"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-jHkVzv dyVEVs pf-31_"><span style="font-style: italic;">By the time you finish reading, you’ll know how to save 90% of the space on your phone or tablet in minutes.</span></span></h2><p class="sc-eGRUor iAsKXf pf-32_" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-jHkVzv dyVEVs pf-34_">If you use a smartphone, you’re probably familiar with the single most annoying notification that ever existed.<br><br><b>“Your storage is full.”<br></b><br>It always happens at the worst possible moment! One minute you’re trying to record something special, and the next you’re thumbing through ALL your photos and videos looking for something to delete.<br><br><b>Why’s it so hard to fit everything on one device?<br></b><br>It’s simple – <span style="text-decoration-line: underline;">phone companies want you to pay for more storage</span>. Keeping your device’s memory small is a smart way to force you to pay them every month – indefinitely – to use “The Cloud”.<br><br>Seriously – who wants to pay every month for years for storage space? And who’s completely comfortable with their private photos and videos just floating around somewhere in The Cloud?<br><br><span style="font-weight: bold;">Fortunately, there’s a simpler way to reclaim space on your devices.<br></span><br>Thanks to a little-known IT company in the Midwest, there’s another option – a “photo stick” for <span style="font-weight: bold;">safely storing your photos and videos</span> somewhere other than your device.&nbsp;<br> 
